# HR Employee
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: HR — the master-data record other HR/cross-app processes reference (leave
# requests, tickets, org charts); Manager is a self-reference hierarchy, same
# tree/rollup option as Case 9's Chart of Account
# Case 18 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
#
# Deliberately light-touch: Case 2 (Leave Request) already IS an HR process. This
# case adds only what Case 2 didn't need — the Employee master itself. Payroll
# calculation is explicitly out of scope: same domain-engine boundary Study 6 drew
# for posting derivation (multi-step, conditional, tax-rule-dependent — not a
# metadata concept).

Employee

Fields

- Employee ID : Text
- Name : Text
- Department : Text
- Position : Text
- Manager : Employee
- Hire Date : Date
- Status : Active | Terminated

Constraints

- Employee ID is required.
- Name is required.
- Hire Date is required.

Permissions

HR

- View

Views

- Employee Form : Form
- Employee Directory : List
- Org Chart : Detail
